# Object `pattern` is a regular expression compiled from its `body` and
# `flags`, the object `string.regex.pattern`. Its receiver is the `regex`
# it belongs to. Both the parser of the body and the matcher of a text
# live here, together with the helpers they share, such as `any`,
# `member`, or `sequence`. The helpers are public attributes, since most of
# them are used by more than one other helper, and moving a private one into
# its only user would nest the recursive parser deeper than the linter
# allows. The tests that build a `pattern` directly live here, while the
# tests that go through `compile` and `match` live in `regex.eo`. Only `flag`
# and `worded` stay in `regex`, because `compile` needs them too, so
# `pattern` reads them through its receiver.

